    "summary": "Boy’s gown or boubou (Af1966,01.2b are the matching trousers), made of imported European cotton sheeting, which has been tailored to shape and assembled using a sewing machine. The cotton has been decorated by sewing over the surface a white cotton thread to imitate a damask weave and the pattern formed by lengths of strip-weave sewn together. Two large decorative panels of circles and knots are sewn in yellow imported thread on the front and back, with extensive use of buttonhole eyelet stitching.",
